      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2011 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Elevated levels of stearoyl-CoA desaturase (SCD) activity have been implicated in metabolic disorders such as obesity and type II diabetes. To circumvent skin and eye adverse events observed in rodents with systemically-distributed inhibitors, our research efforts have been focused on the search for new liver-targeting compounds. This work has led to the discovery of novel, potent and liver-selective acyclic linker SCD inhibitors. These compounds possess suitable cellular activity and pharmacokinetic properties to inhibit liver SCD activity in a mouse pharmacodynamic model."
      },
